{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030314-night-horrors-conquering-heroes-errata","id":1030314,"title":"Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes errata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-11T16:44:36-08:00","id":1030314,"title":"Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes errata","content":"Please list any errata you have found in Conquering Heroes.<br /> <br /> Usual rules apply: this is about actual errors. Typos, obvious inconsistencies, text covered by images, missing material, etc. If there's a sentence you personally would have worded differently, that's not errata, that's opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T16:58:52-08:00","id":1030321,"title":"","content":"Willpower is not a stat you add to die pools. Page Specifics coming soon.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pg. 98: Primordial Seas: The Insatiable suffers a -2 penalty to <b>Willpower</b> and Social rolls but gains an additional dot of Strength and Wits. </div> </div> </div>Resistance Rolls, maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pg. 100: The Storyteller then makes an extended and contested roll using the Insatiable\u2019s Strength + Satiety versus the Beast\u2019s Composure + <b>Willpower</b>. </div> </div> </div>Resolve, I assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-11-2017, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:05:57-08:00","id":1030324,"title":"","content":"<b>pp. 2\u20137, opening story: </b>Some of the text is supposed to be bold and/or italic, but the font doesn\u2019t represent it, or it got lost in layout; there\u2019s a few places where the text just doesn\u2019t make sense without some kind of visual differentiation. Mostly it's from page 3 onward, but there might be words before that that are meant to be emphasized. (I think the same error came up in the core with the full page stories; it's the same font). I imagine there's a raw draft to check, but just in case, I think these are the parts that should be offset:<ul><li><i><b>Count the seconds after the thunder.</b></i></li> <li>Vince had time to think <i><b>but you\u2019re dead, Mom</b></i> before he realized she was dead.</li> <li><i><b>Count the seconds after the thunder, and you can tell how far away the</b><b> storm is.</b></i></li> <li><i><b>Yes,</b></i> his mother said, <b><i>that one.</i></b></li> <li><i><b>So many storms, Vincent.</b></i></li> <li><i><b>No,</b> </i>said his mother.<b> <i>But they\u2019re near. Count. Count the seconds, find the storms.</i></b></li> <li><i><b>I\u2019m scared, Mom.</b></i></li> <li><i><b>What?</b></i></li> <li><i><b>You have nothing to be afraid of. They aren\u2019t really real.</b></i></li> </ul><br /> <b>p. 8, Credits: </b>The Editor\u2019s name is missing.<br /> <b>p. 13: </b>The Walt Disney attribution should have an em-dash to conform with the other chapter quotes<br /> <b>p. 13: </b>&quot;Two themes pervade this <b>book;</b>&quot; \u2013 should be a colon<br /> <b>p. 13:</b> &quot;Instead, those who take on these monsters are the heroes and the creatures found within these pages are the ones who need conquering.&quot; <b>\u2013 </b>I can\u2019t parse this. There might be another \u201cwho\u201d missing between <i>pages </i>and <i>are</i>?<br /> <b>p. 20 and 21, sidebars: </b>The font for the headers makes the colon characters invisible.<br /> <b>p. 25: </b>&quot;...her<b> mistress\u2019</b> mental control...&quot; \u2013 should be <i>mistress\u2019s</i><br /> <b>p. 64: </b><i>Heart of Darkness</i> should be in italics<br /> <b>p. 94: </b><i>Warm Bodies</i> should be in italics<br /> <b>p. 94: </b>Behind the big chapter header, there\u2019s another visible header that also says \u201cChapter Three: Insatiable\u201d<br /> <b>p. 98: </b>&quot;...minus -2 penalty to <b>Willpower</b> and Social rolls...&quot; \u2013 Willpower isn\u2019t rolled; should be Resolve + Composure? <b>Edit</b>: From what Satchel wrote, I think it's supposed to be Resolve.<br /> <b>Back cover: Ugalla </b>should be Ugallu","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-12-2017, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:48:31-08:00","id":1030353,"title":"","content":"p.48: &quot;Shepherd's Gaze&quot; references Nightmares triggering when a sleeper wakes; unless the wording in the Beast core rulebook was meant differently, a delayed Nightmare takes effect when its target next goes to sleep. Also, the dice pool for the power does not specify whether the Finesse Attribute used is the Hero's highest Finesse Attribute or uses an Attribute that is fixed when gaining the Gift, and as a contested power the Beast's Lair should contribute to the opposing roll.<br /> <br /> p.74-75: The Empyrean Swimmer has Bane Sense, but its bane as described is not a valid bane as the ephemeral being mechanics define it and it cannot be used in most of the ways banes are used \u2014 most notably, it is not something that the Swimmer can touch and suffer damage from. As written, it's an extra ban.<br /> <br /> p.98 and 100: Willpower is listed as an individual component of multiple dice pools; most &quot;Willpower rolls&quot; in the established system are rolls of Resolve + Composure, as Willpower is not normally a rolled Trait and rolls that use the Willpower pool's current total, though rare, are typically explicit about this rather than risk confusion by naming an Attribute Task with a derived Trait. Further, the pool to contest Subversion of Contentment is listed as Composure + Willpower, which is unclear as to whether this means Resolve + Composure + Composure or Composure + Current Willpower.<br /> <br /> p.98: Apart from simplified feeding criteria and the narrative effects of warping their surroundings and attracting supernatural beings, &quot;all the bonuses that a Beast gains during the Merger&quot; are part of a variable set of benefits whose number is determined by the former Lair rating of a Rampant Beast, including any bonuses to detecting ambushes; the Insatiable specifically have a Lair rating of 0 unless they have stolen a Lair from a Beast. If they acquire these bonuses dynamically with the acquisition of a Lair, this should probably be specified.<br /> <br /> p.99: &quot;Impossible Anatomy&quot; refers to &quot;extraordinary success,&quot; which is not an existing systems term. Should be &quot;exceptional success.&quot;<br /> <br /> p.101: &quot;The Insatiable and the Ephemeral&quot; sidebar references ephemeral beings gaining the ability to &quot;sense the presence of the area.&quot; Unless there is a missing word or part of this sentence specifying how this relates to the usual state of Twilight and/or Manifestation Conditions, this phrase does not denote any modification to the normal abilities of ephemeral beings in an area.<br /> <br /> p.102: &quot;Cast Aside&quot; references the Staggered Tilt, which does not exist in any other books and does not have its mechanical effects described. &quot;The Burning&quot; does likewise with the Paralyzed Tilt. Existing Tilts like Stunned or Immobilized or Insensate may be mechanically analogous, but new Tilts should ideally have at least some mechanical description.<br /> <br /> p.103: &quot;We Can See Your Insides&quot; references the &quot;Sickened&quot; Tilt. If this is not mechanically analogous to the &quot;Sick&quot; Tilt (as inflicted by entering a Den) or the effects of the &quot;fetid aura&quot; imbued by Foul Mess, this is the same problem as exists in the Esurients listed on p.102 above.<br /> <br /> p.105 and 112: Terminological inconsistency in character descriptions. &quot;Horrific form&quot; instead of &quot;Horrible Form.&quot;<br /> <br /> p.112: Colette's Moment is listed as &quot;Frozen Hell&quot; despite that Moment being called &quot;Freezing Hell&quot; everywhere else in the chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:21:33-08:00","id":1030421,"title":"","content":"<b>Bookmarks: </b>The first bookmark titles the book as &quot;Night <b>Horros</b>&quot;<br /> <b>p. 9: </b><b>the </b>Silversmith -- <i>the </i>should be capitalized<br /> <b>p. 9: </b>\u2014Lightseeker -- needs a space after the dash<br /> <b>p. 9:</b> \u2014the Dream Killer -- space after dash<br /> <b>p. 10:</b> <b>the </b>Sentinel -- caps<br /> <b>p. 11:</b> <b>the </b>Unrelenting Clown -- caps<br /> <b>p. 11:</b> <b>the </b>Blitz Boy -- caps<br /> <br /> <b>p. 100: </b>&quot;The Storyteller then makes an extended and contested roll using the Insatiable\u2019s Strength + Satiety versus the Beast\u2019s Composure + <b>Willpower</b>. For each point of Satiety above 5 the Beast has, her player receives a -1 penalty to her roll, and for each point below 5, he receives a +1 bonus. <b>For each success the Insatiable achieves, they move the Beast\u2019s Composure or Presence down by 1. </b>When both Attributes reach zero, the Insatiable successfully subverts the Beast\u2019s consciousness and gains control for one hour for each point of Satiety the Beast has.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's unclear what the Beast's contested roll is meant to do here: is it meant to subtract successes from the Insatiable's successes? If so, that isn't the default resolution for contested rolls (the CofD core actually specifically says that's not how it works). It doesn't say what happens if the Beast exceeds the Insatiable; as written, the Beast isn't actually doing anything. And technically, this should be a resisted roll (subtracting a Resistance Attribute from the Insatiable's pool) since number of successes count; that's the rule of thumb.<br /> <br /> Also, as Satchel noted above, Willpower is almost never rolled, especially paired with one of its own constituent Attributes. Perhaps it's meant to be Resolve + Composure (Resolve + Lair would also make sense, as it's more fitting with the way contested powers usually work).<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> From the system on the same page below, it seems that the intent <i>is </i>that the Beast is subtracting successes, but it should probably be clarified for the above (and what happens if the Beast wins), as it comes first. And Willpower + Lair is probably meant to be Resolve + Lair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-12-2017, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:41:15-08:00","id":1030430,"title":"","content":"(Could a mod sticky this thread?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T03:53:44-08:00","id":1030511,"title":"","content":"Page 72, should Cru have either a Lair trait or Nightmares?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T06:55:38-08:00","id":1030553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pg. 24: The subsequent media coverage of her untrained, but astute, <b>massage</b> of victims\u2019 emotions became a hit. </div> </div> </div>That should be message, though I'm having fun figuring out what exactly is going on with this particular phrasing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T07:29:50-08:00","id":1030572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pg. 26: During a busy lunch rush at a diner, Danny found himself sharing his booth space with a stranger who seemed to be allergic to silence, a cute <b>twentysomething</b> who introduced himself as Ben. </div> </div> </div>twenty something<br /> <br /> EDIT: Apparently not a typo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-12-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:02:09-08:00","id":1030707,"title":"","content":"On page 51, in the bottom right-hand corner: &quot;his bodyguard, an <b>Alakim </b>who used. . .&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:12:45-08:00","id":1030714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030314-night-horrors-conquering-heroes-errata?p=1030511#post1030511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 72, should Cru have either a Lair trait or Nightmares?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a Rampant Beast, so no. They lose those in the Merger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:14:25-08:00","id":1030718,"title":"","content":"The sidebar on p.112 makes it look like the Ventrue vampire suffers from the Masquerade weakness (specific type of prey) rather than the actual Requiem one (aloofness making it easier to lose touchstones).<br /> <br /> It's been 12 years lads. Time to update your notes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: not sure if it belongs in the errata or not, but how is Colette suppose to freeze her victims to death? Her Moment doesn't give her any such powers. One way around this would be to give her a Lair with the appropriate Trait, but since she needs to steal one, she couldn't have it when she killed her parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","user":"Daigotsu Max","date":". 01-12-2017, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T14:15:23-08:00","id":1030787,"title":"","content":"On page 91, Tears on the Sand has Increased Awareness listed as an Atavism when it's in fact an effect of the Merger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T00:26:27-08:00","id":1031034,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 5: </b>&quot;Somewhere <b>in room</b> he couldn\u2019t see...&quot; -- missing an <i>a</i><br /> <b>p. 25: </b>&quot;When she does profile an innocent-seeming brood, childlike Beast, or <b>unobtrusive Lair</b>...&quot; -- Lairs can't really be obtrusive, as they aren't physical places in the material world; they're only in the Primordial Dream. If Candy profiled a Lair, it would be overtly magical and otherworldly, which would be out of tone with her concept.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-13-2017, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T07:07:48-08:00","id":1031138,"title":"","content":"Luca Rohl is said to be an Eshmaki in his writeup, but an Ugallu in his character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T15:43:55-08:00","id":1031358,"title":"","content":"p. 15 -- When describing the Insatiable in the introduction, the sentence &quot;These creatures capture and take over those with any connection to the Primordial Dream before they come to realization as either Beasts or Heroes.&quot; doesn't match with the description given of their origins at the beginning of the chapter (particularly how, to quote the chapter, 'A Beast is born feeling that she is different...' '...but an Insatiable manifests suddenly and without prediction.').<br /> <br /> p. 94 -- The paragraph starting with &quot;No one knows what act inspires the Insatiable&quot; is a little unclear, as the word 'Insatiable' seems to be used used both to describe the character as a whole and also their analog to the Horror. If that's intentional, that it sort of means both, it could be clearer.<br /> <br /> p. 96-97 -- While most of the chapter references a singular Primogenitor as an origin for the Insatiable, there is some unclear stuff under 'The Moments' that implies the existence of (or at least belief in) multiple Primogenitors or some other 'founder' of each Moment. One sentence implies that a given Moment may consider itself to have come from another Primogenitor, but this seems at odds with the rest of the chapter. Also, while the text goes out of its way to say that each Moment has its own view of the Primogenitor, only two of the Moment descriptions reference this in any way and one strongly suggests multiple Primogenitors. <br /> A particular sentence that stands out as unclear is &quot;Each <i>Primogenitor</i> is a place out of history and an era that defined the birth of the <i>Primordial Dream</i>.&quot; (emphasis mine) In the context of the paragraph, 'Primogenitor' feels like it should probably be 'Moment.' 'Primordial Dream' doesn't seem to fit with the sentence in context, and it's unclear what that should be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, notably, there are multiple references throughout the chapter of Insatiable being able to unleash their true forms 'in the same manner as the Beasts,' (to quote one example) heavily implying that the Insatiable can transform in the physical world. Thing is, though, Beasts don't change into an alternate form outside of their Lair or dreams, so maybe this needs clarified. On a related note, there's the 'Horrible Form' ability on page 99 (one of the aforementioned references) and then the 'Terrible Form' Esurient on page 103 and it feels like one started off as the other and some wires got crossed along the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:54:01-08:00","id":1032275,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 59, sidebar: &quot;Cherion </b>Group&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T14:31:30-08:00","id":1032325,"title":"","content":"Pg 83-84: Alvin Zane's history describes 